@ [manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cpms_i03b_faithful_json_byte_ingress\Source_Document_Manifest.sop

& [SourceIntegrity] passed at 8061 bytes SHA256 8CD89C290173FFFFF227FF0B3F14D5AE14694527636F38D73214ED7B2C247629
& [Baseline] is pushed commit 2b8af816cc6cac11673e9b8f16dc4cbc8aa22bd6
& [FormationAuthority] exists because byte-ingress semantics are validator independent
& [ImplementationAuthority] is absent because I03B has no activation source signature or phase lock

& [Correction1] chooses BTreeMap rather than an unresolved set-or-map alternative
  + duplicate detection must retain the first key offset
  + each open object therefore owns BTreeMap decoded_name to first_key_offset
  + insertion order is not inferred from map order; original bytes remain ordering authority

& [Correction2] defines deterministic fault precedence
  * input byte bound
  * forbidden BOM
  * complete UTF-8 validation
  * empty or whitespace-only input
  * JSON lexical structural duplicate and resource scan
  * trailing non-whitespace data
  + first fault in this gate order is authoritative and later gates do not run

& [Correction3] identifies the selected Unicode profile
  + RFC 8259 grammar permits escape sequences that can encode unpaired surrogates in observed deployments
  + Cantor's faithful identity profile rejects unpaired surrogate escapes to guarantee decoded Unicode scalar identity
  + this is a deliberate stricter profile and must not be represented as universal parser behavior

& [Correction4] closes name equality
  + equality is exact decoded Unicode scalar sequence
  + escape spelling differences collapse when they decode to the same sequence
  + Unicode normalization case folding locale and confusable mapping do not occur
  + this prevents silent identity rewriting while still detecting syntactically escaped duplicates

& [Correction5] separates limit scopes
  + object members array items and scalar values are aggregate document counts
  + member-name maximum is per decoded name in UTF-8 bytes
  + numeric-token maximum is per source token in bytes
  + input bytes and path depth provide aggregate upper bounds on retained names and fault paths

& [Correction6] closes offset and EOF meaning
  + every offset is zero-based from the first supplied byte
  + token spans are half-open start inclusive end exclusive
  + an EOF grammar fault uses offset equal to input byte length
  + a duplicate key offset names the opening quote of each member-name token

& [Correction7] prevents partial authority
  + scanner internal frames names tokens and accounts are provisional until the complete trailing-data gate passes
  + any fault drops all provisional state and returns only one closed fault
  + accepted instance owns an exact byte copy so later readers share stable immutable content

& [Correction8] limits stable diagnostics
  + stable code grammar_class path offset limit and observed fields carry identity
  + human explanation is bounded advisory text
  + implementation-specific debug or parser display messages never enter proof comparison

& [Correction9] closes source touch at formation level
  + proposed future implementation touches tool lib.rs one new json_ingress.rs and one new integration test
  + no Cargo change is needed because cantor_core already exports sha256_bytes and the standard library supplies the scanner structures
  + exact line and module collision audit remains an activation prerequisite

& [AuditDisposition] is source_valid_after_corrections_formation_allowed_implementation_forbidden
